{
 "_doc": "Camera overrides for render_job.py (three.js metres, Y-up). hero_auto: apartment hero stills (living/bedroom/bathroom) are re-framed by ray-casting the furnished room (clear foreground, long view, window in frame; door leaves of that room hidden). 'shots' entries override any field of a shot after that (position, lookAt, lens_mm, clip_start, auto:false to keep the exported/explicit camera, hide:[object-name substrings]). 'extra_exterior' / 'extra_common' add shots. 'hero_per_package': packages whose hero stills use their own exported framing (cameras.json unitsData.<unit>.packages.<pkg>.hero) instead of the package-independent one. Extra shots may carry variant_of / variant_tod: the manifest then also attaches them as variants.<tod> of that base shot. 'heroes': explicit hero-still cameras per unit (id = <unit>-living|bedroom|bathroom), merged over the exported hero of the same id for EVERY package and mood; hide_doors hides the door leaves (+ ironmongery) of the shot's room (roomId, plus hide_rooms). 'variant_of': {shot id: [base shot id, tod]} - the manifest folds those shots into variants.<tod> of the base entry.",
